&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Req ID: 3273572924&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":336761,"name":"Customer Success EMEA","child_ids":[],"parent_id":268135}],"offices":[{"id":3963,"name":"London","location":"London, United Kingdom","child_ids":[],"parent_id":23658}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://www.mongodb.com/careers/job/?gh_jid=8301805","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":true}],"internal_job_id":3589523,"location":{"name":"United States"},"metadata":[{"id":22194060,"name":"Position ID","value":"10007422","value_type":"short_text"},{"id":24918,"name":"Department ID","value":"D43920-Influencer Marketing","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":22194061,"name":"Team","value":"T10156-Customer Marketing","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4914027,"name":"Region","value":"North America","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4137836,"name":"Working Model Eligibility","value":["2-Flexible"],"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":4914029,"name":"Job Level","value":"People Manager","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":24109,"name":"Employment Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":1073551,"name":"Job Type","value":"Standard","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":988684,"name":"JD Link","value":"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nEpVAgRP4Wopli4k1GKm6T7buJE7nNMFppBtCxUlJcU/edit?tab=t.rq6uqdja52xw#heading=h.yn8utdyp54rk","value_type":"url"},{"id":5525802,"name":"Baseline Budgeted Salary","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":5525816,"name":"Other Large Market Budgeted Salary","value":{"unit":"USD","max_value":"174000.0","min_value":"122000.0"},"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":13324394,"name":"Job Post Range (United States)","value":{"unit":"USD","max_value":"226000.0","min_value":"115000.0"},"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":40497768,"name":"Job Post Range (Canada)","value":{"unit":"USD","max_value":"0.0","min_value":"0.0"},"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":57694516,"name":"Job Post Range (Poland)","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":64002488,"name":"Job Post Range (Italy)","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"}],"id":8301805,"updated_at":"2026-10-27T16:24:13-04:00","requisition_id":"3273589523","title":" Director of Customer Marketing & Advocacy","company_name":"MongoDB","first_published":"2026-10-23T09:06:25-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is hiring a Director of Customer Marketing &amp;amp; Advocacy to showcase our customers and support one of our strongest growth levers. This is a build-and-influence role: you will scale customer marketing into a strategic growth function impacting market share, mindshare and awareness with a focus on enterprise segments and AI-native startups.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re not looking for someone to run customer marketing as usual. We want a leader who will innovate, drive change, and take this program to the next level: an AI-enabled engine that finds, matches, and activates customer voice at speed and scale, and a program other companies point to as the bar they aspire to. You will replace manual, ad hoc processes with automation and AI, so customer stories reach every channel faster and with less friction and innovate the customer marketing function and model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build a world where our customers show up everywhere: on stage, in analyst and press conversations, across our brand campaigns and content, and throughout the buying journey. You will also create a channel for customer insight where the insight we gather from customers will sharpen how Product and Product Marketing position, message, and launch. You will make sure every one of those moments is planned, measured, and tied to corporate goals. Customer voice will be the foundation of MongoDB&#39;s brand, building awareness and mindshare with the buyers and builders who matter most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead the customer marketing team across AMER and EMEA and partner closely with Brand, Communications, Strategic Events, Social Media, Product Marketing, Executive Programs, Sales, Customer Success, Partners, Product, and Investor Relations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role can be based remotely in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Put customer voice at the center of MongoDB&#39;s story, across every channel&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make the customer voice the heart of our brand. Partner with Brand Marketing &amp;amp; Creative to make customer outcomes a foundational part of MongoDB&#39;s brand narrative and campaigns, building awareness and mindshare and shaping how the market sees us&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead customer storytelling and content. Set the editorial bar for case studies, video, and executive point-of-view content, and make sure those stories feed brand, social media, communications, events, and demand programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring customers to every stage. Partner with Strategic Events to make customers central to flagship events such as MongoDB.local, plus keynotes, webinars, and brand activations, recruiting and preparing customer speakers who bring our story to life&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Earn credibility beyond our own channels. Work with Communications to connect customers with the press, analysts, and industry influencers who shape enterprise and developer opinion, so credible third-party voices carry our story further than we can alone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reimagine the program and build the AI-enabled engine&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Redefine what customer marketing can be, and set the bar. Set the charter, operating model, and multi-year roadmap for a function that unifies storytelling, advocacy, executive engagement, and influencer relationships into one system, and build a program that peers benchmark themselves against&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an AI-enabled engine that scales. Use automation and AI to find, match, and activate customer voice across channels, from story intake and customer matching to content tagging and performance reporting. Replace ad hoc, one-off requests with clear standards, shared ownership across teams, defined dependencies, and accountability for results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow a deep, diverse customer community. Lead the global strategy for recruiting and nurturing customers across enterprise segments and AI-native startups, so we always have the right voice for the moment and the channel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed customer proof across the business. Bring customer evidence into brand campaigns, product launches, demand programs, and sales conversations, so it becomes a dependable part of how we market, launch, and win&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn customer voice into insight. Make customer insight a two-way exchange, not just a channel for outbound proof. Capture what customers tell us through stories and bring it back to Product and Product Marketing to inform positioning, messaging, and launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive impact&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prove the business case. Define KPIs and build the attribution model that connects customer proof to brand awareness and mindshare, revenue growth, retention, and expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence up and across. Build executive sponsorship across Brand, Communications, Social, Events, Sales, Customer Success, Product, Partners, Product Marketing, and Investor Relations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead the team. Set vision, priorities, and metrics; hire, coach, and develop a high-performing global team, including people managers. Own budget, agencies, and the tooling behind the work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of B2B marketing experience, including significant leadership of customer marketing, advocacy, or customer-led brand programs at an enterprise software, cloud, data, or developer-focused company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years leading teams, including managing managers and teams across regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of innovating and driving change: you&#39;ve taken a customer marketing or advocacy program well beyond the standard model, built systems that scale efficiently, and created work your peers and the broader community look to as a benchmark&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using AI and automation to scale customer marketing or advocacy operations, plus a clear point of view on where AI is taking the function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building or scaling a customer marketing function through significant growth or change, with quantifiable results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional storytelling and editorial judgment, with experience making customer voice central to a brand narrative, building awareness and mindshare, and translating complex technology into clear, credible business stories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating customer voice across brand campaigns, communications, social and influencer marketing, events, and product launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success building customer advocacy and co-marketing programs that recruit and engage a strong, diverse base of customer participants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence, with experience engaging C-level customers and changing senior leaders&#39; minds with data and customer evidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building cross-functional operating models with clear ownership, dependencies, and accountability, and influencing stakeholders without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort in a fast-moving, technical, AI-driven market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing to both large enterprises and startups, and to technical buyers or developers as well as executive decision makers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI-enabled advocacy or customer evidence platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting executive communications, keynote development, or large-scale customer events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supplying customer proof for earnings, investor, or analyst materials at a public company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A recognized presence in the customer marketing community, such as conference speaking, advisory boards, industry awards, published thought leadership, or teaching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About MongoDB&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is built for change, empowering our customers and our people to innovate at the speed of the market. We have redefined the data platform for the AI era, enabling builders to create, transform, and disrupt industries with software. MongoDB’s unified data platform, the most widely available, globally distributed data platform on the market, helps organizations modernize legacy workloads, embrace innovation, and unleash AI. Our cloud-native platform, MongoDB Atlas, is the only globally distributed, multi-cloud data platform and is available across AWS, Google Cloud, and Microsoft Azure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With offices worldwide and over 67,000 customers, including AI-native startups and approximately 75% of the Fortune 100, relying on MongoDB for their most important applications, we’re powering the next era of software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our compass at MongoDB is our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company&quot;&gt;Leadership Commitment,&lt;/a&gt; guiding how and why we make decisions, show up for each other, and win. It’s what makes us MongoDB.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To drive the personal growth and business impact of our employees, we’re committed to developing a supportive and enriching culture for everyone. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/culture/employee-benefits-that-make-a-difference-at-mongodb&quot;&gt;From employee affinity groups, to fertility assistance and a generous parental leave policy&lt;/a&gt;, we value our employees’ wellbeing and want to support them along every step of their professional and personal journeys.&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/blog/channel/culture&quot;&gt; Learn more about what it’s like to work at MongoDB&lt;/a&gt;, and help us make an impact on the world!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is committed to providing any necessary accommodations for individuals with disabilities within our application and interview process. To request an accommodation due to a disability, please inform your recruiter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB, Inc. provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type and makes all hiring decisions without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Req ID: 3273589523&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;MongoDB’s base salary range for this role is posted below. Compensation at the time of offer is unique to each candidate and based on a variety of factors such as skill set, experience, qualifications, and work location. Salary is one part of MongoDB’s total compensation and benefits package. Other benefits for eligible employees may include: equity, participation in the employee stock purchase program, flexible paid time off, 20 weeks fully-paid gender-neutral parental leave, fertility and adoption assistance, 401(k) plan, mental health counseling, access to transgender-inclusive health insurance coverage, and health benefits offerings. Please note, the base salary range listed below and the benefits in this paragraph are only applicable to U.S.-based candidates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;MongoDB’s base salary range for this role in the U.S. is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$115,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$226,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;","departments":[{"id":216777,"name":"Influencer Marketing","child_ids":[],"parent_id":6182}],"offices":[{"id":3964,"name":"Austin","location":"Austin, TX, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":23657}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://www.mongodb.com/careers/job/?gh_jid=8274059","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":true}],"internal_job_id":3579829,"location":{"name":"Gurugram"},"metadata":[{"id":22194060,"name":"Position ID","value":"10005349","value_type":"short_text"},{"id":24918,"name":"Department ID","value":"D24020-Chief Info Security CISO","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":22194061,"name":"Team","value":"T10191-CISO","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4914027,"name":"Region","value":"APAC","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4137836,"name":"Working Model Eligibility","value":["2-Flexible"],"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":4914029,"name":"Job Level","value":"People Manager","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":24109,"name":"Employment Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":1073551,"name":"Job Type","value":"Standard","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":988684,"name":"JD Link","value":"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ssDnJaw9T9raTmiRyvAzcFfRTW7_EGyAQrrzCKWjgO8/edit?usp=sharing","value_type":"url"},{"id":5525802,"name":"Baseline Budgeted Salary","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":5525816,"name":"Other Large Market Budgeted Salary","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":13324394,"name":"Job Post Range (United States)","value":{"unit":"INR","max_value":"0.0","min_value":"0.0"},"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":40497768,"name":"Job Post Range (Canada)","value":{"unit":"INR","max_value":"0.0","min_value":"0.0"},"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":57694516,"name":"Job Post Range (Poland)","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":64002488,"name":"Job Post Range (Italy)","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"}],"id":8274059,"updated_at":"2026-10-27T16:24:13-04:00","requisition_id":"3273579829","title":"Director of Global Security Operations","company_name":"MongoDB","first_published":"2026-10-16T10:18:15-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;MongoDB&#39;s Global Security Organization (GSO) is looking for a Director of Global Security Operations to build and lead GSO&#39;s first dedicated team in India. This is a foundational leadership role: your first mandate is to stand up a 20-person team from scratch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This team’s first mission will be extending US based teams in three different areas:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vulnerability management - AI driven detection, triage and workflow management of vulnerabilities from code to components to applications to infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launch readiness - shifting security analysis left to proactively address security needs as far upstream from product launch as possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Core enterprise security - projects focusing on improving protection against insider threats and and newly emerging AI Governance and Security needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking to speak to candidates who are based in Gurugram for our hybrid working model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who We Are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GSO secures MongoDB&#39;s products, infrastructure, and the trust our customers place in us — spanning product security, corporate security, and risk, and working across engineering, go-to-market, and corporate development to keep security moving at the same speed as the business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, hire, and onboard a 20-person team including 3 managers - across vulnerability management, launch readiness, and core enterprise security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up the operating rhythms, tooling, and documentation the India team needs to work as a first-class part of GSO from day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get new hires productively engaged quickly and working seamlessly with required stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively manage matrix reporting, ensuring ambiguity doesn&#39;t slow the team down — resolve competing priorities between local and functional leadership before they become the team&#39;s problem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the India team&#39;s capacity, constraints, and growth needs back to GSO leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the durable leadership bench and processes that let the India team operate as an accountable, outcome-owning part of GSO going forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead an inclusive, high-performing global team by setting clear goals and operating rhythms; coaching and developing talent through regular, candid feedback and career conversations; monitoring team health and engagement; recognizing strong performance and addressing performance concerns early and fairly; and communicating change early with clarity and context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in security operations, security engineering, or a related technical discipline, including at least 5 years in a people-leadership role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Information Security, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct, hands-on experience in at least one of: vulnerability management, security automation or workflow tooling, or enterprise security operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of hiring and ramping a technical team quickly while holding the line on quality and culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating successfully in a matrix structure — with the judgment to manage functional dotted-line relationships without losing ownership of your own team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with a mandate that will evolve as the team matures — you&#39;re building this job as much as filling it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and relationship-building skills across geographies and time zones spanning the US, EMEA, and India&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t feel that you meet all of the requirements? We encourage you to apply anyway — studies show strong candidates sometimes rule themselves out prematurely. MongoDB has a diverse, inclusive, equitable, and high-performing environment, and we want to keep improving our ability to deliver for customers.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to Haves&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background specifically in vulnerability management platforms, security orchestration/automation (SOAR) tooling, or enterprise security operations at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a matrix organization with international, distributed reporting lines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Success in This Role Means&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The India team is fully staffed and operating to MongoDB&#39;s standards for quality, pace, and culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to step into direct delivery level accountability vs. extending capabilities of other teams once the initial team build phase is complete&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The India GSO team has moved from a build-phase support function to owning clear, accountable delivery in vulnerability management, workflow automation, and enterprise security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About MongoDB&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is built for change, empowering our customers and our people to innovate at the speed of the market. We have redefined the data platform for the AI era, enabling builders to create, transform, and disrupt industries with software. MongoDB’s unified data platform, the most widely available, globally distributed data platform on the market, helps organizations modernize legacy workloads, embrace innovation, and unleash AI. Our cloud-native platform, MongoDB Atlas, is the only globally distributed, multi-cloud data platform and is available across AWS, Google Cloud, and Microsoft Azure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With offices worldwide and over 67,000 customers, including AI-native startups and approximately 75% of the Fortune 100, relying on MongoDB for their most important applications, we’re powering the next era of software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our compass at MongoDB is our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company&quot;&gt;Leadership Commitment,&lt;/a&gt; guiding how and why we make decisions, show up for each other, and win. It’s what makes us MongoDB.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To drive the personal growth and business impact of our employees, we’re committed to developing a supportive and enriching culture for everyone. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/culture/employee-benefits-that-make-a-difference-at-mongodb&quot;&gt;From employee affinity groups, to fertility assistance and a generous parental leave policy&lt;/a&gt;, we value our employees’ wellbeing and want to support them along every step of their professional and personal journeys.&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/blog/channel/culture&quot;&gt; Learn more about what it’s like to work at MongoDB&lt;/a&gt;, and help us make an impact on the world!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is committed to providing any necessary accommodations for individuals with disabilities within our application and interview process. To request an accommodation due to a disability, please inform your recruiter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is an equal opportunities employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Req ID: 3273579829&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":85949,"name":"Chief info Security CISO","child_ids":[],"parent_id":371021}],"offices":[{"id":65909,"name":"Gurugram","location":"Gurugram, Haryana, India","child_ids":[],"parent_id":23659}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://www.mongodb.com/careers/job/?gh_jid=8077491","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":true}],"internal_job_id":3499593,"location":{"name":"United States"},"metadata":[{"id":22194060,"name":"Position ID","value":"10015442","value_type":"short_text"},{"id":24918,"name":"Department ID","value":"D42010-Partner Programs","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":22194061,"name":"Team","value":"T10450-VAR-TECH & AI Programs","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4914027,"name":"Region","value":"North America","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4137836,"name":"Working Model Eligibility","value":["2-Flexible"],"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":4914029,"name":"Job Level","value":"People Manager","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":24109,"name":"Employment Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":1073551,"name":"Job Type","value":"Standard","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":988684,"name":"JD Link","value":"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HFSytAihg8XAge5HAhxGGSTuqE92_UEA1iBHsu2_ojE/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.8ld5wmvkgyuw","value_type":"url"},{"id":5525802,"name":"Baseline Budgeted Salary","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":5525816,"name":"Other Large Market Budgeted Salary","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":13324394,"name":"Job Post Range (United States)","value":{"unit":"USD","max_value":"192000.0","min_value":"192000.0"},"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":40497768,"name":"Job Post Range (Canada)","value":{"unit":"USD","max_value":"0.0","min_value":"0.0"},"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":57694516,"name":"Job Post Range (Poland)","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":64002488,"name":"Job Post Range (Italy)","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"}],"id":8077491,"updated_at":"2026-10-27T16:24:13-04:00","requisition_id":"2273499593","title":"Director, Partner Programs","company_name":"MongoDB","first_published":"2026-07-24T16:29:53-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;MongoDB&#39;s Partner Program is how we formalize value for every partner type in our ecosystem — Technology/ISV partners, Services and Solutions partners (including our Systems Integrators), Cloud partners (AWS, Azure, Google Cloud), Built with MongoDB partners, and Certified by MongoDB DBaaS partners. We&#39;re looking for a Director, Partner Programs to own this program end to end: the tiering and benefits structure, the incentive framework, certification (including our SI Associate and SI Architect tracks), and the operational rigor that keeps thousands of partners engaged and productive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll report to the VP of Partner Strategic Operations and oversee all MongoDB Partner Programs globally, managing a team of Partner Program Managers. You&#39;ll be the connective tissue between the field-facing work being done in Sales Plays &amp;amp; Offerings, the platform work being built by our Business Product Manager (PRM), and the automation work coming out of Digital Process &amp;amp; AI Operations — making sure the underlying program itself stays coherent, well-governed, and aligned to company strategy as all of that activity happens around it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role can be hybrid near any of our MongoDB hub offices in the United States or remote in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own Partner Program strategy and structure&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve the overall architecture of the MongoDB Partner Program across all partner categories — Technology, Services and Solutions, Cloud, Built with MongoDB, and Certified by MongoDB DBaaS — including tiering, entitlements, and benefits at each level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the program structure stays aligned to MongoDB&#39;s broader GTM strategy, including emerging priorities like AI-driven partnerships and cloud marketplace growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own partner certification pathways (e.g., SI Associate and SI Architect certifications) and ensure they reflect current MongoDB technology and sales priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design and govern incentives&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the global partner incentive framework — MDF, SPIFs, rebates, and co-sell incentives — ensuring programs are compliant, scalable, and clearly tied to desired partner behaviors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with the Sales Plays &amp;amp; Offerings lead to evaluate and structure incentives behind specific sales plays and joint offerings, translating field-level recommendations into funded, governed programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track incentive ROI and make the call on which programs to scale, adjust, or sunset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage program operations and team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a team of Partner Program Managers, each responsible for one or more partner categories, setting priorities and holding the team accountable to program health metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end partner journey at the program level: onboarding, tiering/qualification, certification, renewal, and escalation resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Enablement to make sure certification and program content stays current and effectively delivered to partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner across the ecosystem function&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the Business Product Manager, PRM to ensure program rules (tiering logic, entitlements, certification tracking) are accurately reflected and enforced in the PRM platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Digital Process &amp;amp; AI Operations to identify where program administration (qualification, renewals, claims processing) can be automated or enhanced with AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Partner Programs in planning and strategy conversations with the VP of Partner Strategic Operations and other Partner org leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Measure and report&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own program-level KPIs: partner activation and tier distribution, certification completion, program-driven pipeline and revenue, and partner satisfaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver regular program health reporting and business reviews to the VP and other executive stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to continuously refine program design — what&#39;s driving partner engagement and revenue, and what isn&#39;t&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in partner/channel programs, alliances, or partner marketing at a B2B SaaS or infrastructure/data company, with at least 3+ years managing a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of owning a multi-tier partner program end to end — design, launch, governance, and ongoing evolution — ideally spanning multiple partner types (ISV, SI/services, cloud/marketplace)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience designing and governing partner incentive programs (MDF, SPIFs, rebates) with clear ROI discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud marketplace partner programs (AWS, Azure, GCP) and how they interact with a vendor&#39;s own partner program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional leadership — comfortable partnering with sales, enablement, product, legal, and finance to keep a global program running smoothly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with PRM platforms (Salesforce PRM, Impartner, Workspan, or similar) and how program rules get operationalized in them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence: experience presenting program strategy and results to senior leadership and adjusting based on executive input&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people-management skills, with experience developing and prioritizing the work of a small team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running or scaling a partner certification program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in database, cloud infrastructure, or developer-focused technology markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with a dedicated PRM product owner or digital/AI operations function on program automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What Success Looks Like in the First Year&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A validated, leadership-endorsed Partner Program architecture (tiers, benefits, certification) across all partner categories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A governed incentive framework with clear ROI tracking, including at least one incentive built jointly with the Sales Plays &amp;amp; Offerings lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A well-functioning team of Partner Program Managers with clear ownership across partner categories and a healthy operating cadence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established, trusted working relationships with the Business Product Manager (PRM) and Digital Process &amp;amp; AI Operations lead, with program logic accurately reflected in the platform and at least one program process automated&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About MongoDB&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is built for change, empowering our customers and our people to innovate at the speed of the market. We have redefined the data platform for the AI era, enabling builders to create, transform, and disrupt industries with software. MongoDB’s unified data platform, the most widely available, globally distributed data platform on the market, helps organizations modernize legacy workloads, embrace innovation, and unleash AI. Our cloud-native platform, MongoDB Atlas, is the only globally distributed, multi-cloud data platform and is available across AWS, Google Cloud, and Microsoft Azure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With offices worldwide and over 67,000 customers, including 75% of the Fortune 100 and AI-native startups, relying on MongoDB for their most important applications, we’re powering the next era of software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our compass at MongoDB is our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company&quot;&gt;Leadership Commitment,&lt;/a&gt; guiding how and why we make decisions, show up for each other, and win. It’s what makes us MongoDB.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
