e":"short_text"},{"id":24918,"name":"Department ID","value":"D88310-Procurement","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":22194061,"name":"Team","value":"T10128-Procurement","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4914027,"name":"Region","value":"North America","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4137836,"name":"Working Model Eligibility","value":["3-Fully Remote"],"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":4914029,"name":"Job Level","value":"People Manager","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":24109,"name":"Employment Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":1073551,"name":"Job Type","value":"Standard","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":988684,"name":"JD Link","value":null,"value_type":"url"},{"id":5525802,"name":"Baseline Budgeted Salary","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":5525816,"name":"Other Large Market Budgeted Salary","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":13324394,"name":"Job Post Range (United States)","value":{"unit":"USD","max_value":"149000.0","min_value":"76000.0"},"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":40497768,"name":"Job Post Range (Canada)","value":{"unit":"USD","max_value":"0.0","min_value":"0.0"},"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":57694516,"name":"Job Post Range (Poland)","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":64002488,"name":"Job Post Range (Italy)","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"}],"id":8224592,"updated_at":"2026-10-27T16:24:13-04:00","requisition_id":"3273559477","title":"Senior Manager, Procurement","company_name":"MongoDB","first_published":"2026-10-14T14:08:54-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is looking for a Senior Manager, Procurement (Software) to support our growing company&#39;s needs. This role requires a strategic thinker, but also someone who is prepared to “roll up their sleeves.” It also requires interaction across the organization, globally. The right candidate will be a builder with strong analytical, negotiation and communication skills. &amp;nbsp;This position will work in the Procurement Team managing procurement analyst and supporting the company in creating and implementing a category strategy for global Software. This role is based in the New York office and will be reporting to the Head of Procurement &amp;amp; Travel who is also based in New York. By joining the MongoDB Procurement team you will be gaining an enormous amount of experience while accelerating your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based remotely in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,0,0&quot;&gt;Serve as the main point of contact for global Software contracts, leading category strategic initiatives and managing a team of procurement analysts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,1,0&quot;&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally across the organization with stakeholders and the global Legal team to ensure vendor compliance and requirements are met&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,2,0&quot;&gt;Develop and execute a Software Category Management strategy and roadmap aligned with company growth and technology goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,3,0&quot;&gt;Own and manage a pipeline of software renewals, sourcing initiatives, and supplier engagements, ensuring proper planning and execution across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,4,0&quot;&gt;Build a deep understanding of software spend, market trends, licensing models, and supplier landscapes to unlock cost savings and value optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,5,0&quot;&gt;Establish trusted partnerships with key stakeholders in Finance, Legal, IT, Security, and business teams to guide procurement decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,6,0&quot;&gt;Partner with global teams across regions and time zones, including regular collaboration during Pacific Time business hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,7,0&quot;&gt;Drive supplier negotiations, vendor performance management, and sourcing activities to secure optimal commercial outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,8,0&quot;&gt;Ensure all deals within your scope comply fully with the company purchasing policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;So, what does success look like?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Manager&amp;nbsp; will be successful in this role when they can start executing the following strategic tasks and responsibilities after their first quarter with the company:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,0,0&quot;&gt;Deliver superior and consistent project management skills for multi country, cross functional team projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,1,0&quot;&gt;Work closely with global stakeholders on pre renewal strategy, RFP distribution, contract negotiations, and post renewal analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,2,0&quot;&gt;Develop a trusted advisor relationship with key business partners and internal stakeholders through effective communication, strategic guidance, and high quality execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,3,0&quot;&gt;Build and maintain a forward looking software renewal and sourcing pipeline with clear visibility into risks, opportunities, and upcoming business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,4,0&quot;&gt;Develop actionable category strategies based on spend analysis, supplier insights, and business priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,5,0&quot;&gt;Identify and deliver measurable cost savings, cost avoidance, and value optimization opportunities across the software portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,6,0&quot;&gt;Contribute to the development of new tools, processes, and approaches that support global expansion and operational scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,7,0&quot;&gt;Develop an understanding of the legal framework for contract execution and supplier risk management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,8,0&quot;&gt;Lead and grow the team with career planning, mentorship, and professional development at the forefront&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About You&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,0,0&quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree or MBA/Master&#39;s Degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,1,0&quot;&gt;8+ years of experience within an indirect procurement team, including significant experience managing software purchasing and supplier negotiations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,2,0&quot;&gt;4+ years of people management experience required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,3,0&quot;&gt;Experience developing category strategies and managing complex software supplier relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,4,0&quot;&gt;Ability to analyze spend data, draw conclusions, and develop actionable recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,5,0&quot;&gt;Strong organizational and project management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,6,0&quot;&gt;Legal contract experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,7,0&quot;&gt;Demonstrated ability to build strong stakeholder relationships and influence decision making across multiple business functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,8,0&quot;&gt;Highly articulate with excellent verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,9,0&quot;&gt;Ability to work effectively with global teams and stakeholders across multiple time zones, including Pacific Time business hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,10,0&quot;&gt;Think creatively, are highly driven, and are skilled at creating structure in situations that are uncertain or ambiguous within a rapidly growing business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;0,11,0&quot;&gt;Demonstrated ability to roll up your sleeves and work alongside team members, driving projects through to completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;About MongoDB&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is built for change, empowering our customers and our people to innovate at the speed of the market. We have redefined the data platform for the AI era, enabling builders to create, transform, and disrupt industries with software. MongoDB’s unified data platform, the most widely available, globally distributed data platform on the market, helps organizations modernize legacy workloads, embrace innovation, and unleash AI. Our cloud-native platform, MongoDB Atlas, is the only globally distributed, multi-cloud data platform and is available across AWS, Google Cloud, and Microsoft Azure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With offices worldwide and over 67,000 customers, including AI-native startups and approximately 75% of the Fortune 100, relying on MongoDB for their most important applications, we’re powering the next era of software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our compass at MongoDB is our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company&quot;&gt;Leadership Commitment,&lt;/a&gt; guiding how and why we make decisions, show up for each other, and win. It’s what makes us MongoDB.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To drive the personal growth and business impact of our employees, we’re committed to developing a supportive and enriching culture for everyone. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/culture/employee-benefits-that-make-a-difference-at-mongodb&quot;&gt;From employee affinity groups, to fertility assistance and a generous parental leave policy&lt;/a&gt;, we value our employees’ wellbeing and want to support them along every step of their professional and personal journeys.&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/blog/channel/culture&quot;&gt; Learn more about what it’s like to work at MongoDB&lt;/a&gt;, and help us make an impact on the world!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is committed to providing any necessary accommodations for individuals with disabilities within our application and interview process. To request an accommodation due to a disability, please inform your recruiter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB, Inc. provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type and makes all hiring decisions without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Req ID: 3273559477&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;MongoDB’s base salary range for this role is posted below. Compensation at the time of offer is unique to each candidate and based on a variety of factors such as skill set, experience, qualifications, and work location. Salary is one part of MongoDB’s total compensation and benefits package. Other benefits for eligible employees may include: equity, participation in the employee stock purchase program, flexible paid time off, 20 weeks fully-paid gender-neutral parental leave, fertility and adoption assistance, 401(k) plan, mental health counseling, access to transgender-inclusive health insurance coverage, and health benefits offerings. Please note, the base salary range listed below and the benefits in this paragraph are only applicable to U.S.-based candidates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;MongoDB’s base salary range for this role in the U.S. is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$76,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$149,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;","departments":[{"id":85953,"name":"Procurement","child_ids":[],"parent_id":38842}],"offices":[{"id":95825,"name":"Remote New York","location":"New York, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":23657}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":null},{"absolute_url":"https://www.mongodb.com/careers/job/?gh_jid=7782383","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":true}],"internal_job_id":3405919,"location":{"name":"Austin; Chicago; New York City; Palo Alto; San Francisco"},"metadata":[{"id":22194060,"name":"Position ID","value":"10014885","value_type":"short_text"},{"id":24918,"name":"Department ID","value":"D87200-Recruiting","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":22194061,"name":"Team","value":"145-Recruiting Operations","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4914027,"name":"Region","value":"North America","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4137836,"name":"Working Model Eligibility","value":["2-Flexible"],"value_type":"multi_select"},{"id":4914029,"name":"Job Level","value":"People Manager","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":24109,"name":"Employment Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":1073551,"name":"Job Type","value":"Standard","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":988684,"name":"JD Link","value":"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wTsPohjSbF07mGP-P7E_2oN9lUlN0LaUJ4T3bmwO5_M/edit?tab=t.0","value_type":"url"},{"id":5525802,"name":"Baseline Budgeted Salary","value":{"unit":"USD","max_value":"200000.0","min_value":"140000.0"},"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":5525816,"name":"Other Large Market Budgeted Salary","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":13324394,"name":"Job Post Range (United States)","value":{"unit":"USD","max_value":"220000.0","min_value":"112000.0"},"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":40497768,"name":"Job Post Range (Canada)","value":{"unit":"USD","max_value":"0.0","min_value":"0.0"},"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":57694516,"name":"Job Post Range (Poland)","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"},{"id":64002488,"name":"Job Post Range (Italy)","value":null,"value_type":"currency_range"}],"id":7782383,"updated_at":"2026-10-27T16:24:13-04:00","requisition_id":"1273405919","title":"Senior Manager, Recruiting Operations","company_name":"MongoDB","first_published":"2026-04-09T16:49:25-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is looking for a technical people-first, and execution-obsessed leader to lead the Recruiting Operations team. As the operational backbone of Talent Acquisition, the RecOps team establishes and maintains the foundational infrastructure that makes scalable, high-velocity hiring possible.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Manager of Recruiting Operations, you are the visionary leader responsible for partnering with key stakeholders to build these crucial operational frameworks. You will drive the overarching vision, strategy, and execution across three core areas: process optimization and operational rigor, RecTech modernization and tooling strategy, and predictive talent intelligence and trusted data architecture. By establishing this infrastructure, you will empower TA to consistently find, interview, and achieve the best possible hiring outcomes for the organization. This leadership role demands an exceptional individual with strong technical aptitude, deep data and insights experience, and a proven track record of workflow redesign. You will empower your team to continuously refine the systems, tools, and processes used to support recruiting and hiring teams, ultimately ensuring a scalable and successful hiring environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the RecOps Team: Drive the vision and strategy for the CoreOps team, aligning your roadmap with overall Talent Acquisition (TA) and business goals. You will take full ownership of the three core sub-pillars, taking an innovative and bold approach to identifying and executing large-scale transformation initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the TA Tooling Roadmap &amp;amp; RecTech Modernization: In partnership with HR Tech, establish and oversee the TA technology stack and vendor relationships. You will actively manage the TA tooling roadmap with our Recruiting Product Manager, leading the discovery, implementation, onboarding, offboarding, and systematic, data-focused evaluation of tools. This includes hands-on experimentation with automations and co-leading our AI strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion Predictive Talent Intelligence: Partner with People Analytics to advance the use of recruiting analytics and define key metrics of success. While you will oversee long-term data integrity and self-service reporting, you must also be highly hands-on—using Google Sheets and advanced formulas to manipulate data, generate actionable insights, and provide ad-hoc reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize Processes &amp;amp; Workflows: Redesign core recruiting processes to improve operational rigor across the hiring lifecycle. You will act as a strategic thought partner, working closely with cross-functional People Team partners to ensure that your redesigned workflows operate seamlessly in line with other broader People processes and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Governance &amp;amp; Compliance: Own TA Policy, Governance, and Compliance as a horizontal pillar across all initiatives and in alignment with our broader security, legal and people teams. You will define and oversee official guidelines, standards, and oversight (e.g., Global Recruiting Policy, Approval Hierarchies, Data Privacy) to guarantee control and adherence to all laws (e.g., EEO/OFCCP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject matter expert and strategic thought partner, utilizing deep knowledge of the internal and external hiring landscape to lead and drive key operational projects with cross-functional teams. This ensures solutions adapt to evolving business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance and mentorship to your team, acting as an exceptional leader who plays an active role in guiding and upleveling individuals. You will foster the professional development of a relatively junior team while ensuring deliverables are aligned with the overarching TA strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven Leadership Experience: 5+ years of experience with a proven history of leading and executing complex recruiting operations initiatives, complemented by 3+ years of people management and excellent coaching and development skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Aptitude &amp;amp; Tooling Expertise: Deep expertise with core recruiting technologies (e.g., Greenhouse, Gem, Metaview). You have a demonstrated track record of managing a TA tooling roadmap, evaluating tool ROI systematically, sunsetting redundant platforms, and successfully experimenting with automations and AI in recruiting workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflow Redesign &amp;amp; People Team Alignment: Proven operational rigor and strategic planning aptitude. You are highly experienced at redesigning complex processes and collaborating deeply with People Team partners to ensure seamless system, policy, and process alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-On Data Fluency: You don&#39;t just rely on BI tools like Tableau; you are highly proficient in Google Sheets and comfortable using formulas to independently pull, interpret, and communicate data for ad-hoc reporting and root-cause diagnostics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independent &amp;amp; Autonomous Execution: You are an independent, results-driven leader who operates autonomously. You take full ownership of your team&#39;s execution, deliverables, and outcomes across all high-priority initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance Familiarity: Familiarity with TA Policy, Governance, and Compliance, with a focus on monitoring and addressing the evolving state of global laws and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Relationship Building: You have a track record of successfully partnering and influencing cross-functional partners, stakeholders, and varying levels of leadership. You are a strong relationship builder who enjoys communicating and collaborating effectively across a wide range of functional teams and audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About MongoDB&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is built for change, empowering our customers and our people to innovate at the speed of the market. We have redefined the database for the AI era, enabling innovators to create, transform, and disrupt industries with software. MongoDB’s unified database platform, the most widely available, globally distributed database on the market, helps organizations modernize legacy workloads, embrace innovation, and unleash AI. Our cloud-native platform, MongoDB Atlas, is the only globally distributed, multi-cloud database and is available across AWS, Google Cloud, and Microsoft Azure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With offices worldwide and over 60,000 customers, including 75% of the Fortune 100 and AI-native startups, relying on MongoDB for their most important applications, we’re powering the next era of software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our compass at MongoDB is our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company&quot;&gt;Leadership Commitment,&lt;/a&gt; guiding how and why we make decisions, show up for each other, and win. It’s what makes us MongoDB.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
