&lt;p&gt;Atlas Clusters Security builds the security experience that Atlas customers depend on for mission-critical applications. Across the organization we own cluster networking, data encryption, database authentication, and related controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits on the Encryption &amp;amp; Compliance team. We own Encryption at Rest with customer-managed keys (Bring Your Own Key) across AWS, Azure, and GCP, including private networking to customer key management systems. We also own the security and compliance work that lets Atlas serve highly regulated markets, including government offerings and internal credential management. You will design and operate these systems in production, lead fleet-wide rollouts, and partner with customers when encryption or key-management issues hit their clusters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role can be based remotely within the U.S. in the Pacific, Mountain, or Central time zones only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and design new features for MongoDB Atlas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to and lead complex technical projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with product and design teams, considering the user’s perspective while building technical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with customers and support engineers to fix issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with team members to develop our codebase, best practices, and design principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn from and mentor other team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join an on-call rotation to support Atlas’ production services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;We’re looking for someone who&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has at least 5 years of professional software development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is skilled at writing large-scale, distributed backend systems in a compiled language (Java, Go, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has experience with at least one major cloud provider (AWS, Azure, GCP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has led the launch of a new feature and maintained it in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is eager to solve tough problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has excellent communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is curious, collaborative, and motivated&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: experience with cloud key management (KMS / Key Vault / Cloud KMS), IAM, private networking, or encryption in a production SaaS environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Success Measures&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In 3 months, you&#39;ll have shipped code into production and collaborated with the team to solve tough problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In 6 months, you&#39;ll have contributed to a large project and joined our on-call rotation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In 12 months, you&#39;ll have designed new features, led development work, and become a go-to expert on Encryption at Rest, customer-managed keys, or a related part of the system&lt;/li&gt;
